Next.js serves static assets from this directory. It is empty today — the app uses no
static files — but `frontend/Dockerfile` copies it unconditionally (`COPY --from=builder
/app/public ./public`), which is the standard Next standalone layout. Without this file the
directory does not exist in git, the COPY fails, and `docker compose up web` dies with
"/app/public: not found" — so `make up`, the first command in the README, could never bring
up the web service. Vercel builds from source and never runs this Dockerfile, which is why
the deployed site worked and the break stayed invisible.
